## Getting Used to TypeScript

Before this module, most of my programming experience was with languages such as Python, C++, and some JavaScript. TypeScript felt familiar because it is based on JavaScript, but at the same time it added more structure to the way I had to write my code. At first, having to think about types felt like extra work. After using TypeScript more, I started to understand why having those rules can actually make programming easier.

One of the biggest differences I noticed was being able to tell TypeScript exactly what kind of data I expect. For example, I can create a function like this:

```typescript
function addNumbers(x: number, y: number): number {
  return x + y;
}
